cer.py` are all created.\r\n- The single deviation from the plan template (`step()` raises `RuntimeError` instead of returning `False` when no plan is set) is a strict improvement � it fails fast and is explicitly tested by `TestWaypointSequencerNoPlan`.\r\n- `_completed` and `_current_idx` are always incremented together (semantically \"done\" vs \"next\"), making `_completed` derivable from `_current_idx`. However, this follows the plan template exactly and carries a clear conceptual distinction; it does not rise to a blocking finding.\r\n- No genuine YAGNI/DRY issues that should send the task back to Dev.\r\n===\r\n"}],"details":{}}}
